# ARXOS component registry  —  name  git-url  branch  [type]
#
# WHAT ARX ACTUALLY READS (corrected 2026-09-09): the NAME field only.
# Installs and update checks now go through the R2 index, not git: arx-core
# ops::tools() downloads sha256-verified archives from tools.json, and
# updates::tools_outdated() compares that index against /var/lib/arxos/tools/<name>.
# Neither reads the url/branch/type columns (see ops.rs arxos_tool_bins: it takes
# split_whitespace().next() and nothing else). arx uses the names here to
# health-check the installed tool binaries.
#
# So the git-url / branch / type columns below are LEGACY TEXT, no longer consumed.
# Some still point at `-dist` repos that were never created (arxos-browser-dist,
# arxos-greeter-dist). Do NOT "fix" those URLs expecting update behaviour to change —
# it will not; both of those tools already update fine via R2. Likewise the missing
# type on the arxos-greeter line is harmless.
#
# TO ACTUALLY SHIP OR UPDATE A TOOL: publish it to R2 (arxpush tool-publish.sh ->
# tools.json). A name listed here but ABSENT from tools.json cannot receive updates.
# Currently unpublished (no R2 entry, so no updates): arxos-vm-resize, wallpimp,
# arxguard. `arx update` now REPORTS these by name rather than leaving them
# looking managed: see ops::registry_drift. droidB and deathstroke are published. arxburn is the one that does not need
# one: it self-updates from its own GitHub releases (`arxburn update`, and the
# button in its window), which is why its url column points at the real public
# repo rather than a -dist mirror. linux-arxos is expected to be absent — kernels
# update through their own `arx kernel` path and the arxos-kernels manifest.
#
# type: historical only — tool (default) · core (arx/arxctl/arxupd) · kernel (linux-arxos)
arx https://github.com/thearxos/arx-dist main core
arxctl https://github.com/thearxos/arxctl-dist main core
arxupd https://github.com/thearxos/arxupd-dist main core
arxos-vm-resize https://github.com/thearxos/arxos-vm-resize-dist main tool
wallpimp https://github.com/thearxos/wallpimp-dist main tool
anonkit https://github.com/thearxos/anonkit-dist main tool
droidB https://github.com/thearxos/droidB-dist main tool
arxguard https://github.com/thearxos/arxguard-dist main tool
arxos-greeter https://github.com/thearxos/arxos-greeter-dist main
arxos-browser https://github.com/thearxos/arxos-browser-dist main core
arxburn https://github.com/0xb0rn3/arxburn main tool
deathstroke https://github.com/0xb0rn3/deathstr0ke main tool
linux-arxos https://github.com/thearxos/linux-arxos-dist main kernel
